      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed; I prefer this solution as well since it keeps the atlas sub run\u0027s bounds() in the consistent coordinate space as the other geometries (i.e. the RHS of the transform stored on the DrawParams). The additional matrix to capture the original coordinate space is, in some ways of thinking about it, a property of the AtlasSubRun (or the AtlasPath too).\n\nThe common case is a translation, in which case it\u0027d be possible to have the local bounds stored in `AtlasSubRun`, but that\u0027s not a strict requirement. If we had a guarantee on the nature of the transform decomposition (e.g. always up to a 2x2 or 2x3 matrix), we could change the uniform to be the inverse of the sub run\u0027s transform and apply it to the sub run coordinates before they are transformed to device space.",
      "parentUuid": "0798b730_67b5a80b",
      "revId": "19b2e7f46502eb197432fa45d714cb564e2a63ea",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
